<BaseLayout title="Privacy notice — draft" description="Draft privacy information for CashForPhilly inquiries; pending owner and legal review before production." noindex>
  <section><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Draft — not legally approved</p><h1>Privacy notice (draft)</h1><p class="notice">Do not launch lead capture until an authorized owner or legal reviewer confirms this notice, the operator identity, retention schedule, and contact details.</p><h2>Information and purpose</h2><p>Inquiry forms collect your name, contact method, property location and type when applicable, message, optional marketing consent and first-party campaign attribution. This information is used to respond to your inquiry. A fraud-prevention challenge is processed by Cloudflare Turnstile.</p><h2>Processing and access</h2><p>Submissions are stored in a dedicated Cloudflare D1 database accessible to authorized operators. Cloudflare Pages processes the request and Turnstile verifies the challenge. Inquiry data is not automatically enrolled in Constant Contact. If you separately choose a verified Constant Contact signup, that provider processes subscription details under its own terms.</p><h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>Retention duration, deletion/export policy and operator identity require approval before launch. You may request access, correction or deletion using the verified contact channel when published. Optional marketing consent is unchecked by default; no SMS marketing is enabled.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
